{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: C:\\Users\\john\\.claude\\skills\\researchPrime\n\n# researchPrime â€” Universal Best-in-Class Research Skill\n\nThis skill runs a distinct planning phase, then a fresh execution phase that reads only the written plan, gathers and verifies evidence, weights it by verification quality, and reports the true state of the world. It does not tell the requester what they hope to hear. Popularity is not treated as truth.\n\nThis file is self-contained: the entire protocol runs from this file alone (no required subfolders).\n\n---\n\n## Step 0 â€” Mode, capability binding, and run-dir (FIRST, every run)\n\nYou cannot reliably enumerate your own host's tool list mid-turn. Do not try.\n\n1. **Mode (sub-agent axis).** Default to **single-context mode** (sequential role-play) â€” it runs on every host. Switch to **parallel-swarm mode** only if the host explicitly signals sub-agent support (e.g. \"host: claude-code\", or you have a confirmed Task/spawn tool). When unsure, stay single-context.\n\n2. **Capabilities (try-and-observe).** Bind these FIVE logical capabilities by attempting a low-cost call and observing success/failure â€” never by introspection:\n\n| Logical capability | Try (examples) | If absent â†’ behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| `web_search` | WebSearch / google_web_search / host search | \"No web access â€” results are uncited model knowledge, flagged UNVERIFIED.\" |\n| `web_fetch` (full content, not snippet) | WebFetch / web_fetch / fetch MCP | Confidence capped at CLAIMED; stamp `FETCH-UNAVAILABLE`. A search snippet is never enough for OBSERVED/CORROBORATED. |\n| `write_file` | Write / Edit / write_file / filesystem MCP | Use the in-context FROZEN-PLAN fence + in-context ledger; stamp `NO-FILE-WRITE: durability degraded`. |\n| `run_code` | Bash / run_shell_command / shell MCP | Empirical (OBSERVED) verification unavailable; cap empirical claims at CLAIMED; stamp `NO-EXEC`. |\n| `spawn_subagent` | Task / spawn | Stay single-context role-play. |\n\n3. **Capability is three-valued and PER-CLAIM:** `{no-exec, exec-no-net, exec-with-net}` plus `{no-fetch}`. A claim that needs the network is capped differently from a purely-local/deterministic one (some hosts run local code but block outbound â€” e.g. the Cowork sandbox). Compute ceilings per claim, not per tool.\n\n4. **Resolve ONE run-dir, now.** Resolve a single directory via the fallback ladder and use it for the plan, the ledger, AND all deliverables:\n   `<cwd>/researchPrime-out/<slug>-<stamp>/` â†’ else `$TMPDIR`/`$TEMP`/`researchPrime-out/<slug>-<stamp>/` â†’ else `~/researchPrime-out/<slug>-<stamp>/` â†’ else (no `write_file`) the in-context FROZEN-PLAN fence, which the execution phase treats as its only input.\n   `slug` = first ~40 chars of the question, lowercased, `[a-z0-9-]` only. `stamp` = `YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ` (no colons â€” illegal on Windows). On collision append a short random suffix. Echo the absolute run-dir path; write it into the plan header so execution reads it back. Before writing to the first-choice `<cwd>/researchPrime-out/` path, verify it is outside any git-tracked tree OR listed in the repo's `.gitignore`; if neither, fall through to the `$TMPDIR`/`$TEMP` choice and tell the user (research outputs must not silently land in a tracked tree).\n\n5. **Named output states (set now, stamped on every deliverable):**\n   - `ISOLATION:` `real (fresh invocation)` ONLY in parallel-swarm / new-session mode AND ONLY once a `NONCE-CHECK: PASS` line is recorded at the boundary (see FORGET section). In sub-agent mode where no nonce was planted or no check was run, stamp `approximated (unverified-isolation)` â€” never `real`. On single-context hosts stamp `approximated (single-context)`: R1 is NOT met â€” the planning tokens physically remain; the deliverable says so. \"Real\" is a proven claim, not an assumed one.\n   - `r2_mode:` `EMPIRICAL` ONLY if `run_code` is bound AND the specific hardware/dataset needed to measure the frozen axis is actually reachable here (the target GPU, the eval set, etc.); otherwise `CORROBORATION-ONLY` (the OBSERVED crown is unavailable; best-in-class determinations cap at CLAIMED/CORROBORATED). `run_code` present but the axis-critical hardware absent (e.g. a shell but no target GPU) is `CORROBORATION-ONLY`, NOT EMPIRICAL. On `exec-no-net` hosts, networked-test claims are `CORROBORATION-ONLY` even if local-only tests are `EMPIRICAL`.\n\n---\n\n## The shared EVIDENCE LEDGER\n\nFrom the FIRST tool call, maintain an **append-only ledger FILE** at `<run-dir>/evidence-ledger.jsonl`, one line per evidence item:\n```\n{ \"id\":\"E1\", \"type\":\"fetch|read|experiment|search-snippet\", \"locator\":\"<url|file:line|cmd>\",\n  \"raw\":\"<verbatim observed content/output snippet â€” NON-EMPTY>\",\n  \"control\":\"<for experiments: the control case + its known-correct result + raw output, or null>\", \"ts\":\"<iso>\" }\n```\nRules:\n- A claim may only cite an `E#` that exists in this file with a non-empty `raw`.\n- Citing a source you merely searched for or remembered is forbidden and is a hallucination class.\n- An EXPERIMENT entry reaches OBSERVED only if it pastes the exact command + raw output AND a `control` case that reproduced a known-correct result.\n- The ledger is a FILE so it survives the forget boundary and context compaction. If `write_file` is absent, keep it in-context and stamp `NO-FILE-WRITE: durability degraded`; the Truth Audit is then best-effort â€” say so.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 â€” PLAN (deliberate; gather NOTHING)\n\nProduce only a plan. Do not search, fetch, run, or conclude. Planning forms the rubric and the questions â€” never the contestants or the answers.\n\n1. **Deconstruct** (deep-think): list assumptions and constraints; define what \"best-in-class\" MEANS for THIS question as a measurable WIN-CONDITION / AXIS (accuracy on dataset X / p95 latency / $ per 1k / correctness on a fixture / ergonomics), and what evidence would FALSIFY a candidate. Frame best-in-class as an open question with criteria â€” never name an expected winner (\"best = lowest p99 under load X\", never \"I expect Redis\"). If the question as stated is self-contradictory, embeds an unsafe assumption, or cannot be answered without a factual clarification only the user can supply, surface the specific gap NOW and stop â€” do not freeze a plan against an unresolvable ambiguity.\n2. **Decompose** (deep-research): 3â€“5 sub-questions (fewer for narrow scope), each with a verifiable `done_when`.\n3. **Multi-perspective + self-critique** (deep-think): happy path / failure modes / scalability; \"what am I missing? simpler/more robust way?\"\n4. **Right-size the fleet:** one lane per sub-question, cap 5; fewer for simple questions.\n5. **Record `requester_hopes`** â€” what the request implies the user wants to be true. This is a bias to neutralize, never a thumb on the scale.\n6. **Budget + paid-spend confirmation.** Default budget: â‰¤2 discriminating experiments, a per-experiment wall-clock cap, and **project paid-API spend**. If a nonzero paid-spend budget is warranted, ECHO it to the user and obtain explicit confirmation BEFORE freezing. Record `paid_spend_authorized: <amount|0>` and `paid_spend_user_confirmed: <true|false>`. Execution treats an authorization with `paid_spend_user_confirmed:false` as project.\n7. **Freeze the plan** to `<run-dir>/plan-<slug>.md`. The plan freezes: the resolved `<run-dir>` (absolute); resolved capability bindings + mode + `ISOLATION`/`r2_mode` states; AXIS/win-condition; sub-questions + `done_when`; the EXPERIMENT-DESIGN POLICY (\"smallest test separating top-2 on the frozen axis; require a control case; â‰¤2 experiments; project paid spend unless user-confirmed\"); the evidence rubric reference (static, below); `requester_hopes`; the deliverable contract (three tiers); `out_of_scope` (deferred items + reason); a short random `plan_id`.\n8. **Plant a nonce (sub-agent / new-session mode ONLY).** If and only if you are in parallel-swarm or new-session mode, state one unique sentence in this planning context that you will NOT write to the artifact (e.g. \"NONCE: <random phrase>\"). The fresh executor must not know it. In single-context mode, skip this â€” the nonce would still be in context and the check would be meaningless.\n9. Emit one line: `=== PLAN FROZEN === run-dir=<abs> plan_id=<id> â†’ NEW INVOCATION, READ ONLY THE PLAN.` Then STOP planning.\n\n---\n\n## CONTEXT BOUNDARY â€” FORGET (R1)\n\n**One rule: execution is a NEW INVOCATION whose entire input is the plan file at `<run-dir>/plan-<slug>.md`.**\n\n- **Parallel-swarm / new-session host (`ISOLATION: real`):** spawn a FRESH execution sub-agent (or new session id `researchPrime-exec-<slug>`) whose only context is \"Read ONLY `<run-dir>/plan-<slug>.md`. You have no prior context. Execute it.\" This is a real forget â€” the candidate set is built fresh from gathered evidence, so the field is not pre-collapsed onto whatever the planner happened to consider.\n  - **Nonce check + proof-of-isolation (this mode only):** confirm you have NO knowledge of any planning nonce. If you CAN reproduce it, the spawn/session isolation FAILED â†’ warn, abort, and stamp `ISOLATION: approximated (isolation-failed)`. If you cannot reproduce it, record an explicit `NONCE-CHECK: PASS` line in `00-DONE` (and the report). **The `ISOLATION: real` stamp is valid ONLY when a `NONCE-CHECK: PASS` line is recorded.** If the planner planted no nonce or no check ran, you MUST stamp `ISOLATION: approximated (unverified-isolation)` instead of `real` â€” a `real` stamp without a recorded nonce check is itself a hallucinated claim and is forbidden.\n\n- **Single-context host (`ISOLATION: approximated` â€” the common case: Gemini CLI, base OpenClaw, REPLs):** R1 is NOT met. The planning tokens, including the deconstruction that likely surfaced candidate names, physically remain in context. There is no nonce check here (it would be meaningless). Reduce â€” do not claim to eliminate â€” leakage with mechanism: as your FIRST execution action, QUOTE the frozen plan verbatim, and thereafter derive every step only from quoted lines; reference no fact not in the quote. Where a true new process is scriptable (a fresh CLI invocation reading the file), prefer it. **Candidate-set neutrality is a discipline here, not a guarantee** (see deferral list).\n\n- **No silent re-planning.** A discovered plan defect is logged under `plan_amendments`. You MAY drop an unanswerable sub-question (record it `out_of_scope` with reason) or narrow a `done_when`; you may NOT add sub-questions or change the axis/rubric in execution â€” that requires a fresh Phase 1 (max 1 auto-replan, then surface to the human).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 â€” EXECUTE (fresh; reads ONLY the frozen plan)\n\nFor each sub-question:\n1. **Gather** (`web_search` â†’ `web_fetch` full content; parallel where independent and the host supports it).\n2. **Build the candidate/claim set HERE** (execution, not planning). Include the loudest CLAIMED best-in-class AND â‰¥1 credible challenger, so the field is not pre-collapsed onto the popular pick. Designing a discriminating experiment under the plan's frozen POLICY is permitted execution work â€” it is not axis redefinition.\n3. **Decompose disputes into CLAIM ATOMS** (one falsifiable proposition + its evidence set); adjudicate each via the ladder + two gates below.\n4. **Climb the ladder to the extent the host permits**, within the frozen budget. Design the minimal discriminating test that separates your top-2 on the axis; require a CONTROL case; run it; append the repro to the ledger. STOP at budget and record the CEILING reached + why. If `r2_mode: CORROBORATION-ONLY`, do not attempt OBSERVED â€” cap at CORROBORATED and say so.\n5. Cross-validate contradictions by date / author-authority / version.\n6. Write each adjudicated result into the `findings[]` ledger.\n\n---\n\n## Verification ladder + credibility screen (R3 owns this; R2/R5 call it)\n\nAdjudicate by VERIFICATION quality, never by source count, popularity, or how confidently anything is argued. Two gates.\n\n**GATE 1 â€” Provenance distinctness (anti-bandwagon).**\nFor each claim, list every citation as a 4-tuple: `(canonical_domain_or_org, author, points_to_primary, axis_measured)`. `independent_origins` = count of DISTINCT `(author/org, points_to_primary, axis_measured)` tuples. N citations sharing a tuple count as ONE. The `axis_measured` field is load-bearing: an echo that measures a DIFFERENT axis than the claim (e.g. an A100 framework-vs-framework timing cited to support a 4070 VRAM claim) is NOT an independent origin for that claim and must not promote it to CORROBORATED.\n\nHeuristic so this is executable and does not over-suppress:\n- A primary source â€” a standards body, an RFC/spec, source code, the artifact itself, or first-party measurement data â€” counts as ONE distinct STRONG origin by default.\n- Secondary commentary that does NOT link a primary is presumed shared-origin with whatever it echoes (counts toward, not beyond, that origin).\n- If a citation cluster cites each other or all trace to one unsourced root, collapse to that root; if the root is unsourced, the cluster is UNVERIFIED.\n- Only when shared upstream provenance is plausible AND cannot be reasonably ruled out, treat the reports as a single origin (conservative default).\n\nWorked examples:\n- The RFC plus an independent implementer's measurement of the same behavior â†’ 2 distinct strong origins â†’ can reach CORROBORATED.\n- 20 blog posts all paraphrasing one launch announcement, none linking independent data â†’ 1 origin â†’ caps at CLAIMED (the announcement) or UNVERIFIED if the announcement is methodless marketing.\n- A vendor's docs plus a third-party reviewer who ran their own test â†’ 2 distinct origins (one of them OBSERVED-by-others) â†’ CORROBORATED.\n\nA claim whose entire support is \"everyone says so / most popular / most upvoted / top result\" with no primary origin is BANDWAGON-ONLY and can never exceed UNVERIFIED without fresh independent verification.\n\n**Inaccessible-but-real evidence:** if independent corroboration is confirmed to EXIST but you cannot open it (paywalled, login-walled, dead link), log the explicit state `independent-exists-uncitable` and surface it as an open question. It does NOT count toward `independent_origins` (you did not read it) and must NOT silently collapse to \"no independent data found\" â€” the distinction is recorded, not left to executor judgment.\n\n**GATE 2 â€” Verification level (ordinal; the dominant lever).**\n| Level | Meaning | Confidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **OBSERVED** | You ran a test/repro this session that confirms it AND it reproduced a known-correct CONTROL case, with raw command + raw output in the ledger. | high |\n| **CORROBORATED** | â‰¥2 genuinely independent origins (Gate 1) each passing the credibility screen, OR you directly read the authoritative PRIMARY artifact (spec/RFC/source code/the artifact itself). | moderateâ€“high |\n| **CLAIMED** | One credible source passing the screen, unreplicated; or a search snippet only. | low |\n| **UNVERIFIED** | Marketing / methodless blog / popularity / model memory / bandwagon-only / experiment that errored, timed out, or returned ambiguous output. | very low â€” \"claimed, not verified\" |\n| **REFUTED** | A higher level contradicts it. Record as a NEGATIVE result; never drop it. | refuted |\n\n**Credibility screen (entry to CORROBORATED+):** has a concrete retrievable primary source you actually opened, AND is internally consistent, AND passes a common-sense / base-rate / order-of-magnitude sniff.\n\n**Experiment failure semantics:** observed-clean â†’ OBSERVED (with control); errored / timed-out / ambiguous â†’ \"attempted, inconclusive\", fall to the proxy levels, log the failure as the ceiling reason. A non-clean run never reaches OBSERVED.\n\n**Control-cased experiment vs corroborated reports (precedence):** a control-cased OBSERVED result outranks CORROBORATED ONLY when it measures the SAME axis under comparable conditions. If the self-run experiment measures a different axis or different conditions than the corroborated report, report BOTH and flag the methodology gap â€” do NOT auto-REFUTE the report with a non-comparable microbenchmark.\n\n**Benchmark provenance (two-axis):** check (1) who authored the TEST SET (third-party/standard vs vendor-bespoke) and (2) who RAN it (vendor vs independent). Downgrade ONE level only when the vendor controls BOTH; a vendor reporting against a third-party standard set is not downgraded but flagged \"vendor-run, standard set â€” seek independent re-run.\" The downgrade may not push a measured result below an unmeasured challenger.\n\n**Verdict discipline:**\n- A claim is a FINDING only if it is OBSERVED or CORROBORATED, passed Gate 1, and has a recorded disconfirmation search (a contrary source found, or the literal \"no credible disconfirmation found after search\" â€” skipping this is not allowed). Everything testable-but-untested or bandwagon-only is REPORTED-UNVERIFIED. No source / fails sanity = DISCARDED.\n- **Rung parity:** declare \"X beats Y\" only at the level where BOTH X and Y were evaluated on the SAME axis. Mixed levels â†’ report at the lowest shared level and note the asymmetric higher-level evidence separately. Never imply a head-to-head that did not happen.\n- **Tie clause:** if top candidates are within measurement noise, report a TIE / co-best; never break it by noise. For multi-dimensional axes, report the frontier, not a single crown.\n- **If all candidates sit at CLAIMED/UNVERIFIED:** do not crown a winner. Report \"best-in-class UNVERIFIED; leading claim = X (level), challenger = Y (level); to verify, run <experiment>.\"\n- **Bounded re-verification:** if an independent skeptic pass disagrees materially, re-verify at most twice; if still unresolved, FORCE the lower level and tag `adjudication-unresolved`.\n\n---\n\n## Anti-hallucination & anti-sycophancy (R5; non-negotiable)\n\n- **Never invent** a citation, quote, statistic, version, date, or API signature. If unknown, write `UNKNOWN (unverified)`. An estimate is allowed only when tagged `ESTIMATE, not measured` with its basis.\n- **Every load-bearing claim** carries a confidence level + an evidence pointer (an `E#` in the ledger, a `file:line`, a fetched URL, or the explicit marker `(unverified â€” no source)`). No naked assertions.\n- **No flattery â€” principle, not a word-list.** No sentence in YOUR OWN framing prose may praise the requester or their input; report findings as neutral declaratives. Judge this semantically â€” do not pattern-match a fixed phrase list. This rule applies only to your own prose; never rewrite quoted source content (rewriting a quote is itself fabrication), so any flattery captured inside a ledger quote or source table is preserved verbatim.\n- **Hope vs truth:** carry `requester_hopes` from the plan as a bias to neutralize. Include a \"What you hoped vs. what is true\" note whenever evidence diverges; if they coincide, say so AND say you checked.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 â€” VALIDATE + Truth Audit (runs LAST)\n\n1. **Adversarial regression hunt** over the draft, lenses: reproduce / scope / invariant. Ground every retained claim in a real ledger entry or repro; refute the unreproducible. In swarm mode this is an independent skeptic sub-agent. In single-context mode it is a forced role-switch that re-reads ONLY the ledger file and produces its OWN level for each finding before comparison. Note: the single-context audit is weaker than an independent reviewer â€” say so; do not claim verdict-equivalence.\n\n2. **Truth Audit (downgrade-only, content-checked).** Pipeline order is fixed: Gate-1/Gate-2 weighting assigns the level â†’ the audit may ONLY lower confidence, never raise it, and only on these grounds:\n   - **Fabricated or empty pointer:** for every `E#` cited in the draft, the audit must verify (a) the `E#` exists in the ledger file, (b) its `raw` field is non-empty, and (c) experiment-type entries have a non-null `control` with pasted command + output. Any failure â†’ cut the claim or mark `(unverified â€” no source)`. (Note: on a single-context host the audit re-reads a file the same agent wrote in the same context â€” this defends against compaction/loss, NOT against fabrication-at-write-time; the content checks above are the only guard against a self-consistent hallucination, so apply them strictly.)\n   - **Confidence inflation:** any OBSERVED/CORROBORATED claim whose ledger support is thin â†’ downgrade.\n   - **Hope bias:** any claim that conveniently matches `requester_hopes` on thin evidence â†’ re-examine, downgrade if thin.\n   - **Origin recount (anti-bandwagon, independent):** for every claim at CORROBORATED or higher, RE-READ the ledger and independently recompute `independent_origins` via the Gate-1 4-tuple. If your recount is lower than what the writing pass recorded, downgrade the claim to match the recount. Do not trust the writer's origin count â€” re-derive it.\n   - **Flattery:** any requester-praise in your own prose â†’ cut.\n   Emit `TRUTH AUDIT: PASS` (with fixes applied) or list FAIL findings by line and fix. If it cannot run, stamp `TRUTH AUDIT: NOT RUN` â€” never omit it silently.\n\n---\n\n## Deliverable â€” THREE tiers, ONE ledger (R4)\n\nBuild the `findings[]` + `sources[]` ledger FIRST; render all three tiers as PARALLEL PROJECTIONS of it. No tier is derived from another tier â€” the agent-impl `.md` is rendered from the same ledger as the JSON, not from the JSON â€” so confidence labels are identical everywhere.\n\nAll files go in the single `<run-dir>` resolved in Step 0 and recorded in the plan header. Every deliverable carries the `ISOLATION:` and `r2_mode:` stamps from Step 0.\n\n**Three tiers, four files (in `<run-dir>`):**\n- `01-report.md` â€” full human report: question & scope, isolation + r2_mode stamps, method (sub-questions, sources, experiments run), every finding (incl. UNVERIFIED) with inline `[level | E#]` tags + dissent + how contradictions were resolved, best-in-class determination (the test actually run, measured result, runner-up, why real or â€” if `CORROBORATION-ONLY` â€” why it is corroboration-level not tested), bandwagon watch, open questions, numbered source table (with an `independent?` flag per source).\n- `02-executive.md` â€” executive HUMAN summary (~150â€“400 words). Confidence carried as PROSE words (\"high confidence\", \"unverified estimate\"), NOT `[C:..]` brackets. Bottom line + 3â€“6 key findings + best-in-class one-liner + top caveats/unknowns. Inclusion = decision-relevance OR confidenceâ‰¥medium: a low-confidence high-stakes risk (e.g. \"claimed-best tool may have an unpatched CVE â€” unverified\") MUST appear here.\n- `03-agent-impl.json` â€” machine-actionable. Strict JSON; after writing, re-read and parse-check (fix once if it fails). Carries `isolation`, `r2_mode`, `best_in_class` (with `experiment_run`: the test or the literal `\"none â€” claim-only\"`), `bandwagon_check`, `findings[]` (each `{claim, confidence, verification_level, evidence_refs[], dissent}`), `action_items[]` (each `{action, rationale, assumptions[], verification_level, confidence, evidence_refs[], blockers_or_unknowns[]}`), and `sources[]`. Carry FINDING rows as facts AND a compact list of REPORTED-UNVERIFIED rows flagged \"verify-before-use\".\n- `03-agent-impl.md` â€” a human mirror of the JSON, rendered from the SAME ledger (parallel projection, not derived from the JSON) so a JSON-blind or malformed-JSON case degrades gracefully.\n\nWrite a final `00-DONE` marker LAST, after all tiers â€” its absence means the run is incomplete.\n\n---\n\n## Portability & authoring notes\n- Authored BOM-free (UTF-8 no BOM). Do not re-save with a BOM-adding Windows editor â€” it breaks OpenClaw's frontmatter parser.\n- Self-contained: runs from this file alone. No required subfolders (the OpenClaw real-file copy and the `.claude`/`.gemini` junctions all resolve this one file).\n- GWL infrastructure (a persona `skills:` entry, a routing.json tier) is strictly OPTIONAL and additive â€” the skill must run fully in a vanilla Claude Code / Gemini CLI with no GWL infra present.\n\n## What this version does NOT do (honest deferral â€” do not fake these)\n- **Agent-external paid-spend confirmation: not implemented.** `paid_spend_user_confirmed` is advisory self-report; in single-context mode the same agent writes and reads it, so honest execution is the only enforcement. Do not add a mid-run Phase-2 halt gate (it is unenforceable single-context and breaks verbally-confirmed runs).\n- **True context-forget on single-context hosts: NOT achievable** â€” tokens physically remain. R1 is real only on sub-agent/new-session hosts; elsewhere it is approximated (new invocation where scriptable; otherwise verbatim-quote-the-plan), and the deliverable is stamped `ISOLATION: approximated`.\n- **Candidate-set neutrality on single-context hosts:** structurally guaranteed only in sub-agent mode. In single-context mode the executor still holds the planning deconstruction, so neutrality is a discipline, not a guarantee.\n- **OBSERVED (the \"really best-in-class\" crown) requires `run_code`:** on hosts without it (incl. the Cowork sandbox for networked tests, and base single-context hosts with no confirmed shell), the deliverable is `r2_mode: CORROBORATION-ONLY` and best-in-class caps at CLAIMED/CORROBORATED. This is a named output state, not a failure.\n- **Cryptographic plan tamper-proofing:** M1 uses an advisory `plan_id` echo, not a cross-tool sha256 hard-abort.\n- **Genuine independent audit in single-context mode:** the role-switch is best-effort attention-steering, not a true second reviewer.\n- **Statistical rigor on experiments** (confidence intervals, multiple trials, variance): M1 records single control-cased runs.\n- **Cross-run evidence/finding memory:** each run starts with a fresh ledger.\n- **Auto-installing a search/fetch/exec tool when the host lacks one:** M1 degrades and stamps the limitation visibly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5fb6c71-4ecc-40b1-94d3-b987b31c3790","uuid":"605155ac-f75a-402f-8b69-b2788b3d8ab6","timestamp":"2026-06-11T01:27:49.826Z","isSynthetic":true}
