bed from source.\n- SQ2 â€” R&D control surface (the major in-flight feature): What is the per-project R&D job system, how complete is it? (rnd_registry.py, job_runner.py, lanes.py, gate_adapter.py, effort_history.py, report_viewer.py, deliverables.py, distro.py, project window, trio integration). done_when: components, data/state files, job lifecycle, and integration points are mapped with completeness assessment.\n- SQ3 â€” Build / test / deps / dev infra: How is it built, tested, verified? Dependency truth. (pyproject, requirements.txt vs stdlib-only claim, tests/ ~34 files, healthcheck, foreman.config, vendor/). done_when: how to run tests, test coverage breadth, dependency reality, and verification mechanisms are stated; pytest result OBSERVED if runnable.\n- SQ4 â€” What's done vs outstanding + history: prior plans, decision logs, TODOs, partial builds, deferrals. (planning/rnd-v1/{MASTER-PLAN,IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN,DECISION-LOG,EXECUTION-LOG,SETUP}, planning/gemini-adapter/PLAN, CLAUDE.md, git log of 39 commits, _archive, _prototypes, _mockups, memory). done_when: a done/outstanding ledger + the key open threads are extracted from primary docs.\n- SQ5 â€” Risks / unknowns (cross-cutting; synthesized by orchestrator from SQ1-4 + targeted checks): runtime fragility (duplicate-supervisor history), security posture (auth token, enable_remote, planted-secret tests), portability/single-context constraints, uncommitted working-tree state. done_when: each risk has an evidence pointer and a severity.\n\n## Experiment-design policy\nSmallest deterministic checks that establish project state: run the test suite (pytest), check git status/log, read primary source. Require the command + raw output in the ledger for OBSERVED. â‰¤2 \"experiments\" beyond reads = (1) pytest run, (2) a server/import smoke check if cheap. Project paid spend = $0; no paid APIs invoked.\n\n## requester_hopes (bias to neutralize)\nThe launch was auto-generated by Anchor's own R&D lane; the implicit hope is \"the project is in good, coherent shape and the R&D feature is basically done.\" Neutralize: report unfinished/fragile/uncommitted state plainly even where it contradicts a tidy narrative.\n\n## Evidence rubric\nStandard researchPrime ladder: OBSERVED (ran it + control) > CORROBORATED (>=2 independent origins or primary artifact read) > CLAIMED (one source) > UNVERIFIED. For a single-repo inventory, reading the primary source file = CORROBORATED (primary artifact); running a command with output = OBSERVED. A claim sourced only to a doc/CLAUDE.md that the CODE contradicts is downgraded to the code's verdict.\n\n## Deliverable contract\n01-report.md (full), 02-executive.md (~150-400w prose), 03-agent-impl.json (strict JSON), 03-agent-impl.md (mirror), evidence-ledger.jsonl, 00-DONE last.\n\n## out_of_scope (deferred + reason)\n- External best-in-class benchmarking â€” N/A for a single-project inventory.\n- Live web research â€” not needed; all evidence is local.\n- Running the live NSSM service / hitting localhost:8777 â€” would touch running infra; read-level + test-suite evidence only (do not mutate working tree / running service).\n- Deep security pen-test â€” surface posture only.\n\n=== PLAN FROZEN === run-dir=C:\\dev\\Anchor\\.anchor\\projects\\227eb089706140388b829776d87e57c8\\research plan_id=anchor-bf-7f3a â†’ NEW INVOCATION, READ ONLY THE PLAN.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":53185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1118},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5fb6c71-4ecc-40b1-94d3-b987b31c3790","uuid":"3f05a427-7885-47ba-93dc-9a038583e774","request_id":"req_011Cbvc38Krc8wAjUgtK9iFN"}
